\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,pathlib\\np=pathlib.Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08')\\nfor n in ['approved-plan.json','review_plan-0.response.json','phase-entry-inventory.json']:\\n d=json.loads((p/n).read_text());print(n)\\n if n=='phase-entry-inventory.json':\\n  print(str(d)[:1100])\\n else:\\n  print(json.dumps({k:d.get(k) for k in ['verdict','summary','issues','residuals']},ensure_ascii=False))\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,pathlib\\np=pathlib.Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08')\\nfor n in ['approved-plan.json','review_plan-0.response.json','phase-entry-inventory.json']:\\n d=json.loads((p/n).read_text());print(n)\\n if n=='phase-entry-inventory.json':\\n  print(str(d)[:1100])\\n else:\\n  print(json.dumps({k:d.get(k) for k in ['verdict','summary','issues','residuals']},ensure_ascii=False))\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"approved-plan.json\\n{\\\"verdict\\\": null, \\\"summary\\\": null, \\\"issues\\\": null, \\\"residuals\\\": null}\\nreview_plan-0.response.json\\n{\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"AGREE\\\", \\\"summary\\\": \\\"AGREE: the plan is executable and appropriately bounded, with correct proposed arithmetic and explicit authority-dependent acceptance conditions. No unresolved material objection to the plan was found.\\\", \\\"issues\\\": [], \\\"residuals\\\": [\\\"Applicable AASB 9 measurement authority and primary ASC/ASBE comparator support remain uninspected; this review establishes no treatment under those sources.\\\", \\\"Mandatory disclosure claims require their own applicable authority; generated financing notes alone do not establish disclosure compliance.\\\", \\\"Revenue, tax, leases, FX, complex groups and excluded bond features remain explicit subsequent work.\\\", \\\"No implementation tests were available to run. Accounting validity, empirical forecast validity, human acceptance and wider MC/G closure remain unestablished. This review changed no files.\\\"]}\\nphase-entry-inventory.json\\n{'scripts/check_accounting_p03.py': '4e98ce93fe5a2c9ba94930c6af8d4cee904121713ad9e6529c0645d45d26241f', 'scripts/reconstruction_v1.py': 'ca38b7e6e96c005a96aaca080ff8a1ef4f57ab5e619f068a03173570e9d2fba8', 'scripts/build_repair_fixtures.py': 'd547424c6bb898adf919a4f5d50fd114bc7e759c78c600b2c9724456fab28b2a', 'scripts/accounting_master_response.schema.json': 'aad6a6c3c2cdfc98728bf450c0350e4b3aff3ea32664038bd73b3f8b7ce7cd6c', 'scripts/accounting_master_support.py': 'f11b64c923cc7e8c9b90384f86bf609b543743abbd144ccacaa041e8192238c4', 'scripts/build_real_case.py': 'fb5eefea5c81913058b9aa6dc2732d263991106501bec83692058d664b45d0eb', 'scripts/build_demo_registry.py': 'd56a5055b0a5714834be188487c35d53ac846b17cc4050b7d9386e69526e764e', 'scripts/acquire_financial_report_corpus.py': 'ce67ffa2c5d11a4bb22b589cc34fab6aa51addc80994b8ad333d71d11ce590d7', 'scripts/test_financial_report_corpus.py': '53b707998401a545d9732329e39ab42ca499e8f6aec674729b13713f54988c93', 'scripts/run_accounting_master.py': '30af9169964e1b3db41a5ceb7f185fbd1c56e2829772a430867b006f2ffa7fd7', 'scripts/check_semantic_preparation.p\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,105p' AGENTS.md && sed -n '1,140p' docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/compound-bond.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,105p' AGENTS.md && sed -n '1,140p' docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/compound-bond.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# AccDSL project instructions\\n\\n## Mission entry point\\n\\nBefore substantive work in this project, read:\\n\\n1. [Mission control](MISSION_CONTROL.md).\\n2. [Requirements and acceptance evidence](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md).\\n3. [Current checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md).\\n4. The gap records relevant to the task:\\n   [initial audit](docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md) and\\n   [expanded mission audit](docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md).\\n5. For the authorised master-program work, read the\\n   [master checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md), executable\\n   phase catalog and current `data/accounting-master/next-plan.md`. The older\\n   corpus checkpoint remains historical evidence; current phase execution is\\n   recorded by the master without rewriting frozen release hashes.\\n\\nThe mission preserves the user's goals across sessions. Current user directions\\nand higher-priority instructions still control. Local documents must not be\\nused to request fresh permission for work already authorised by the user.\\n\\n## Working rules\\n\\n- Identify the MC requirements addressed by each nontrivial plan or work unit.\\n  Audit the plan before implementation, experiments or long diagnostics.\\n- Preserve the full goals while staging execution. A small financing demo,\\n  clean PDF build or six populated research ledgers cannot close requirements\\n  for whole-company representation, research quality or implementation detail.\\n- Distinguish direct user requirements, policy requirements and derived\\n  engineering choices. Do not silently convert a convenient library, model\\n  assumption or stage boundary into an immutable product requirement.\\n- Keep source evidence, interpretations, assumptions, joint history families\\n  and scenario-specific results separate and traceable. Preserve unknowns;\\n  do not invent facts, probabilities, accounting compliance or completeness.\\n- Close gaps with the specified evidence, and update the requirements register\\n  and checkpoint after meaningful changes. Add newly discovered gaps rather\\n  than treating the current list as exhaustive.\\n- Follow the applicable policies under\\n  `/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies`. Preserve unrelated work and the\\n  original paper collection. The existing `.git` marker is not a usable\\n  repository; do not initialise or commit merely to create provenance.\\n- Keep operational mission/checklist material out of the reader-facing\\n  scholarly narrative unless it serves a real implementation-reference purpose.\\n- Apply MC35, the user's internal-preparation-before-paid-review requirement.\\n  Finish feasible source research, facts, calculations, software checks and\\n  document repairs before referring a specific question to a professional.\\n  Supply a proposed answer, exact sources, competing interpretation and checked\\n  consequences. Keep unfinished internal work on the internal queue; “human\\n  review pending” is an acceptance status, not a reason to stop that work.\\n  Ordinary reader feedback need not be purchased from an accounting firm.\\n  No professional engagement, outreach or fees are authorised by this policy.\\n  See `docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md` and the current checkpoint.\\n\\nThe current manuscript is specification-incomplete. Read the checkpoint and\\nrequirements before resuming from an older note that says only final review\\nremains. This file authorises no autonomous background campaign or external\\npublication; it directs work undertaken under the user's active instructions.\\n# Compound bond: issuer classification and settlement\\n\\nStatus: internally checked conditional illustration; actual instrument\\nclassification is not established. MC17, MC19; gaps G4 and G7.\\n\\n## Facts and proposed answer\\n\\nThe issuer receives 100, owes two annual coupons of 5 and principal 100, and\\nthe holder may convert that principal into ten ordinary shares. Currency is\\nthe issuer's functional currency. Assume no fees, other options, contingencies\\nor settlement alternatives; assume the share-conversion feature qualifies as\\nequity. The market yield for otherwise comparable non-convertible debt is\\nassumed to be 10%, not estimated from the example.\\n\\nUnder those conditions the proposed issuer split is liability\\n`5/1.1 + 105/1.1² = 11050/121`, and residual equity `1050/121`.\\nThe exact calculation keeps the components summing to 100. Using the stated\\neffective-interest schedule, liability after coupons one and two is `1050/11`\\nand 100. Interest expense totals `2260/121`, including discount accretion.\\n\\nIssue: debit cash 100; credit liability `11050/121` and conversion equity\\n`1050/121`. Accrual debits interest expense and credits liability; each coupon\\ndebits liability and credits cash 5. At maturity, redemption debits liability\\nand credits cash 100. Conversion instead debits liability and credits issued\\nshare equity 100; the original equity component remains in equity. The\\n[checked journal report](../accounting-dossier-checks.json) preserves both\\nsettlement paths. A 5% comparable yield gives liability 100 as an arithmetic\\nboundary case; it is not evidence that a real conversion option has zero value.\\n\\n## Source and boundary\\n\\n[AASB 132](../../research/standards/aasb132.pdf), pp. 12–14 and 25–26:\\nparagraph 22 describes fixed-number/fixed-amount settlement; 25–27 address\\ncontingencies and settlement choices; 28–32 require the compound split and\\nresidual; AG30 confines this treatment to the issuer, AG31 supplies comparable\\nliability discounting, AG32 supplies no maturity-conversion gain/loss, and\\nAG33–AG35 distinguish early repurchase and induced conversion. Paragraph 31\\nrefers subsequent financial-liability measurement to AASB 9. This dossier's\\naccretion calculation is a declared schedule; it does not fill the missing\\nprimary measurement-source audit by implication.\\n\\nThe PDF's pp. 1 and 5 say the compilation applies to annual periods beginning\\non/after 1 January 2023 and **before 1 July 2026**, incorporating amendments\\nthrough 15 December 2022. Period start determines that condition; a calendar\\n2026 annual period is inside it. The local source is an official Australian\\nIAS-equivalent text with the comparison qualifications on p. 4, not proof of\\nevery jurisdiction's currently adopted version.\\n\\n## Strongest counterargument and remaining internal work\\n\\nA variable share count, cash option, foreign-currency exercise amount, put,\\nreset clause, contingent payment or related guarantee could defeat the assumed\\nclassification. The arithmetic can remain perfectly balanced while the\\nclassification is wrong. Do not apply this issuer example to the holder.\\n\\nFor an actual bond, first retain the complete contract and side agreements,\\nprepare a clause-by-clause settlement table, establish reporting basis and\\nperiod, acquire the applicable primary measurement authority, document the\\ncomparable yield and test early settlement/modification where relevant.\\nUS-GAAP and ASBE classification need their own dated sources. All are internal\\npreparation tasks; do not pay for a reviewer to discover the missing clauses.\\n\\nA later review can ask whether named clauses X/Y change the proposed equity\\nclassification under a cited paragraph, with both proposed treatments and\\ntheir reconciled entries supplied. No actual clause requiring that judgment\\nhas been supplied in the current synthetic example.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,pathlib\\nfor f in ['data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/approved-plan.json','docs/design/research/standards-support.json']:\\n d=json.loads(pathlib.Path(f).read_text()); print(f,list(d) if isinstance(d,dict) else 'list');\\n if 'standards' in f: print(json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False)[:5000])\\nprint('missing',[(p,pathlib.Path(p).exists()) for p in ['scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py','scripts/check_accounting_p08.py','tests/test_accounting_p08.py','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08/authority-and-methods.json','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08/result.md']])\\nPY\\nrg -n 'MC06|MC15|MC17|MC19|MC29|MC30' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,pathlib\\nfor f in ['data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/approved-plan.json','docs/design/research/standards-support.json']:\\n d=json.loads(pathlib.Path(f).read_text()); print(f,list(d) if isinstance(d,dict) else 'list');\\n if 'standards' in f: print(json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False)[:5000])\\nprint('missing',[(p,pathlib.Path(p).exists()) for p in ['scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py','scripts/check_accounting_p08.py','tests/test_accounting_p08.py','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08/authority-and-methods.json','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08/result.md']])\\nPY\\nrg -n 'MC06|MC15|MC17|MC19|MC29|MC30' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/approved-plan.json ['plan', 'review', 'plan_hash']\\ndocs/design/research/standards-support.json ['records', 'blocked']\\n{\\\"records\\\": [{\\\"id\\\": \\\"aasb102\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB102_07-15.pdf\\\", \\\"path\\\": \\\"docs/design/research/standards/aasb102.pdf\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"0d6fb4f59cc6daa7088f25e73542945d346f9c737ca85abf1a164a332bf93c06\\\", \\\"access_date\\\": \\\"2026-10-02\\\", \\\"inspected\\\": \\\"Comparison with IAS 2; paragraphs 23–27, 28–34\\\", \\\"support_scope\\\": \\\"Official Australian adoption; for-profit relevant common text; not a claim about all later amendments\\\", \\\"edition_applicability\\\": \\\"July 2015 issue; paragraph 40 applies to annual periods beginning on or after 2018-01-01, with the stated earlier-application provisions. Later amendments not checked in this pass.\\\", \\\"edition_pages\\\": [1, 10], \\\"preparation_dossiers\\\": \\\"docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"aasb17\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB17_07-17_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf\\\", \\\"path\\\": \\\"docs/design/research/standards/aasb17.pdf\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"153e720cc1eaf7eea47d50463003391ea0433271694dd83a44c54a0e92deaec3\\\", \\\"access_date\\\": \\\"2026-10-02\\\", \\\"inspected\\\": \\\"Comparison with IFRS17; paragraphs 14–24, 32–38, 53–59, 60–70A, 78–82, B126–B127; reinspection of PAA, separate reinsurance recognition/eligibility, presentation and period applicability on 2 October 2026\\\", \\\"support_scope\\\": \\\"Official compiled text; PAA service, gross/ceded and risk-adjustment examples only; no full compliance\\\", \\\"edition_applicability\\\": \\\"Annual periods beginning on or after 2023-01-01 and before 2026-07-01; compiled amendments through 2022-12-15. Applicability uses period start, not the date of this review.\\\", \\\"edition_pages\\\": [1, 5], \\\"preparation_dossiers\\\": \\\"docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"aasb132\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB132_08-15_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf\\\", \\\"path\\\": \\\"docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.pdf\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"5c8ce25447c6186ec49f751bc9e7ad48563caaff542b0e0287f3f7783a480501\\\", \\\"access_date\\\": \\\"2026-10-02\\\", \\\"inspected\\\": \\\"Comparison with IAS32; paragraphs 15–22, 28–32, AG30–AG35\\\", \\\"support_scope\\\": \\\"Official compiled text; issuer compound split and maturity conversion; other classification conditions must be checked\\\", \\\"edition_applicability\\\": \\\"Annual periods beginning on or after 2023-01-01 and before 2026-07-01; compiled amendments through 2022-12-15. Applicability uses period start, not the date of this review.\\\", \\\"edition_pages\\\": [1, 5], \\\"preparation_dossiers\\\": \\\"docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"asbe-reproduction\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/企业会计准则第1号——存货\\\", \\\"path\\\": \\\"docs/design/research/standards/asbe-reproduction.html\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"ef50c4730a0c81f16ee419d63f6cade854dbc9a6a254938d05eeb9d920ebebd6\\\", \\\"access_date\\\": \\\"2026-10-02\\\", \\\"inspected\\\": \\\"Entire reproduced 2006 text, articles 1–22, particularly 14–19\\\", \\\"support_scope\\\": \\\"Unofficial reproduction attributed to Ministry of Finance; official origin/version verification remains pending\\\", \\\"preparation_dossiers\\\": \\\"docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"caterpillar2024\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.annualreports.com/HostedData/AnnualReportArchive/c/NYSE_CAT_2024.pdf\\\", \\\"path\\\": \\\"docs/design/research/standards/caterpillar2024.pdf\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"3a38651c724016bca792bef165fd42bb09d9b033d23718372a2599378768e925\\\", \\\"access_date\\\": \\\"2026-10-02\\\", \\\"inspected\\\": \\\"Note 1.C inventories and Note 8 inventories; note number corrected against the retained PDF on 2 October 2026\\\", \\\"support_scope\\\": \\\"Company-authored report, mirror download; records disclosed US-GAAP LIFO policy, not full ASC330 authority\\\", \\\"preparation_dossiers\\\": \\\"docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/\\\"}], \\\"blocked\\\": [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"FASB ASU2015-11 official PDF\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"403 in default and elevated requests; DART ASC330 primary text requires login; no bypass attempted\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Ministry of Finance standards index\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"502 in default and elevated requests; unofficial text retained with verification pending\\\"}]}\\nmissing [('scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py', False), ('scripts/check_accounting_p08.py', False), ('tests/test_accounting_p08.py', False), ('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08/authority-and-methods.json', False), ('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08/result.md', False)]\\n60:| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\\n79:| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\\n81:| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\\n88:| MC19 | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE with dated treatments, elections and transitions. U1, U3. | Define the supported treatment matrix, rule authority and version selection; show matched economic events under selected genuinely different treatments and identify unimplemented operations. | Partially repaired. Ch. 9 compares FIFO/LIFO/average and records dated rule selection. Selected IAS-equivalent paragraphs inspected in official AASB texts; US LIFO has company-policy evidence only, full ASC authority is blocked, and official ASBE version verification remains pending. Source dossiers record exact edition/period limits and correct Caterpillar inventories to Note 8. G7, G8, G13. The acquired panel now supplies report-level preparation-basis evidence across US GAAP, IFRS-oriented reporting and ASBE; this does not replace dated primary accounting authority. |\\n108:| MC29 | Conduct a broad, technically grounded literature survey beyond the original collection. U3, P. | Inspect relevant primary methods/theory/evaluation/appendices and official code where available; compare direct alternatives; make genuine backward/forward screening, source-specific omissions, corrections and claim support inspectable. | Partially repaired: 179 individual title/metadata decisions across 194 occurrences/72 searches replace generic exclusions; generation rejects unscreened candidates. Mack and selected rule sources add inspected technical support. All-candidate full-text review and later module literature are not complete. G8. |\\n109:| MC30 | Preserve the relevant source library and precise provenance. U3, P. | Archive accessible relevant papers under the required naming convention, retain exact versions/anchors, preserve original files, and document unavailable sources without relying on their uninspected claims. | 32 catalogued paper PDFs verified by hash/page count, with original collection preserved; Apple filings and selected standards archived separately. Version/authority limits and four blocked papers remain recorded. Mechanical integrity does not certify every technical claim. G8. The additional financial-report corpus preserves 244 original versions, source/index/discovery hashes and an append-only attempt history; 192 target slots pass source acceptance. |\\n140:plan; v1 evidence remains preserved. This advances MC01, MC03, MC05, MC19–22,\\n141:MC28, MC30 and MC33–35 without closing semantic, accounting or forecast\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"mkdir -p data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08 docs/design/research/p08-v1\\ncat > data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08/progress.md <<'EOF'\\n# P08 implementation checkpoint\\n\\n2026-10-03. Recovery and structured approved plan/review inspected. The two\\nrequired deliverables, engine, checker and test file are absent. Prior stopped\\nplanning work supplies no implementation evidence. Approved scope is a synthetic\\nissuer compound convertible bond; MC06/15/17/19/29/30 and G4/G7/G8 stay wider.\\n\\n## Pre-execution skeptical audit and evidence contract\\n\\nQuestion: can applicable primary authority support a parameterized, exact issuer\\nlifecycle and same-fact comparison? Comparator: existing compound-bond dossier\\n(arithmetic regression only), independently derived present values and cash flows.\\nPass: inspected applicable recognition/measurement/classification/settlement\\nanchors, parameterized atomic journals, both multi-period settlements, matched\\ninputs and reproducible notes. Vetoes: unsupported authority blocks the affected\\ntreatment; invalid dates, ineligible terms, imbalance, negative funding or state\\nmismatch block implementation acceptance. Source failures do not stop independent\\npreparation. No short check establishes accounting compliance, forecast validity,\\nhuman acceptance, superiority or whole-gap closure. Result and source/hash evidence\\nwill be preserved in authority-and-methods.json and result.md.\\n\\nDefaults audit: annual periods, two coupons, fixed shares, functional currency,\\nno fees/tax/options and 10% comparable yield come from the reviewed synthetic\\nexample (hypotheses, not real-market estimates). Wrong eligibility or yield can\\nproduce balanced but wrong accounting: reject unsupported clauses and independently\\ncheck PV, alternative parameters and authority applicability. Australian for-profit\\nTier 1 basis is a bounded scope choice; check edition and period-start limits.\\nOpening cash/equity 20 is synthetic settlement funding; test insufficient cash and\\natomic rollback. Exact rational arithmetic is an engineering choice; this does not\\nvalidate real currency rounding. Inspection dates do not substitute for effective\\nperiods. Matched comparisons hold economics fixed; absent sources stay unresolved.\\n\\nAudit passes for this bounded plan: no ranking/proxy promotion, source-dependent\\nstops are local, and exact outputs answer only the stated conformance question.\\n\\n## Files and next steps\\n\\nDeclared new files: scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py,\\nscripts/check_accounting_p08.py, tests/test_accounting_p08.py,\\ndocs/design/research/p08-v1/*, and the three permitted P08 files. Existing dossier,\\nshared engines, frozen corpus and protected supervisor files remain preserved.\\nNext: inspect applicable AASB 9, AASB 132 and a legitimate primary comparator;\\nrecord source-specific access outcomes; implement engine, generate cases, test\\nnegative paths and run unittest plus checker --check. All deliverables unfinished.\\nEOF\\npython3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport pathlib,hashlib,json\\np=pathlib.Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9