\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\ntext=Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.txt').read_text()\\nfor start,end in [('3.1.1   An entity','3.1.2'),('3.3.1    An entity','3.3.4'),('4.2.1   An entity','4.2.2'),('5.1.1      Except','5.1.1A'),('amortised cost of a financial    The amount','contract assets'),('effective interest method      The method','fair value')]:\\n i=text.find(start);j=text.find(end,i+len(start));print('page',text[:i].count('\\\\\\\\f')+1, text[i:min(j,i+1450)] if i>=0 else 'missing '+start)\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"page 10 3.1.1   An entity shall recognise a financial asset or a financial liability in its statement of financial position\\n        when, and only when, the entity becomes party to the contractual provisions of the instrument (see\\n        paragraphs B3.1.1 and B\\npage 14 3.3.1    An entity shall remove a financial liability (or a part of a financial liability) from its statement of\\n         financial position when, and only when, it is extinguished – ie when the obligation specified in the\\n         contract is discharged or cancelled or expires.\\n3.3.2    An exchange between an existing borrower and lender of debt instruments with substantially\\n         different terms shall be accounted for as an extinguishment of the original financial liability and the\\n         recognition of a new financial liability. Similarly, a substantial modification of the terms of an\\n         existing financial liability or a part of it (whether or not attributable to the financial difficulty of the\\n         debtor) shall be accounted for as an extinguishment of the original financial liability and the\\n         recognition of a new financial liability.\\n3.3.3    The difference between the carrying amount of a financial liability (or part of a financial liability)\\n         extinguished or transferred to another party and the consideration paid, including any non-cash\\n         assets transferred or liabilities assumed, shall be recognised in profit or loss.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nAASB 9-compiled                                            14                                           STANDARD\\n                                  Authorised Version F2023C00399 registered 02/05/2023\\n\\f\\npage 16 4.2.1   An entity shall classify all financial liabilities as subsequently measured at amortised cost, except for:\\n        (a)       financial liabilities at fair value through profit or loss. Such liabilities, including derivatives\\n                  that are liabilities, shall be subsequently measured at fair value.\\n        (b)       financial liabilities that arise when a transfer of a financial asset does not qualify for\\n                  derecognition or when the continuing involvement approach applies. Paragraphs 3.2.15 and\\n                  3.2.17 apply to the measurement of such financial liabilities.\\n        (c)       financial guarantee contracts. After initial recognition, an issuer of such a contract shall\\n                  (unless paragraph 4.2.1(a) or (b) applies) subsequently measure it at the higher of:\\n                  (i)        the amount of the loss allowance determined in accordance with Section 5.5 and\\n                  (ii)       the amount initially recognised (see paragraph 5.1.1) less, when appropriate, the\\n                             cumulative amount of income recognised in accordance with the principles of\\n                             AASB 15.\\n        (d)       commitments to provide a loan at a below-market interest rate. An issuer of such a\\n                  commitment shall (unless paragraph 4.2.1(a) applies) subsequently measure it at the higher\\n                  of:\\n                  (i)     \\npage 18 5.1.1      Except for trade receivables within the scope of paragraph 5.1.3, at initial recognition, an entity shall\\n           measure a financial asset or financial liability at its fair value plus or minus, in the case of a financial\\n           asset or financial liability not at fair value through profit or loss, transaction costs that are directly\\n           attributable to the acquisition or issue of the financial asset or financial liability.\\n\\npage 44 amortised cost of a financial    The amount at which the financial asset or financial liability is measured at initial\\nasset or financial liability     recognition minus the principal repayments, plus or minus the cumulative\\n                                 amortisation using the effective interest method of any difference between that\\n                                 initial amount and the maturity amount and, for financial assets, adjusted for any\\n                                 loss allowance.\\n\\n\\npage 45 effective interest method      The method that is used in the calculation of the amortised cost of a financial\\n                               asset or a financial liability and in the allocation and recognition of the interest\\n                               revenue or interest expense in profit or loss over the relevant period.\\n\\neffective interest rate        The rate that exactly discounts estimated future cash payments or receipts through\\n                               the expected life of the financial asset or financial liability to the gross carrying\\n                               amount of a financial asset or to the amortised cost of a financial liability.\\n                               When calculating the effective interest rate, an entity shall estimate the expected\\n                               cash flows by considering all the contractual terms of the financial instrument (for\\n                               example, prepayment, extension, call and similar options) but shall not consider\\n                               the expected credit losses. The calculation includes all fees and points paid or\\n                               received between parties to the contract that are an integral part of the effective\\n                               interest rate (see paragraphs B5.4.1–B5.4.3), transaction costs, and all other\\n                               premiums or discounts. There is a presumption that the cash flows a\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport urllib.request,pathlib,json,datetime,hashlib\\nu='https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32023R1803'\\nr={'id':'eu2023_1803','url':u,'retrieved_at':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()};p=pathlib.Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1')\\ntry:\\n with urllib.request.urlopen(u,timeout=25) as f:b=f.read();r.update(status=f.status,final_url=f.url)\\n (p/'eu2023_1803.html').write_bytes(b);r.update(path=str(p/'eu2023_1803.html'),sha256=hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest(),bytes=len(b))\\nexcept Exception as e:r.update(access_status='unavailable',error=str(e))\\n(p/'eu-access.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\\\\\\\\n');print(r)\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport urllib.request,pathlib,json,datetime,hashlib\\nu='https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32023R1803'\\nr={'id':'eu2023_1803','url':u,'retrieved_at':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()};p=pathlib.Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1')\\ntry:\\n with urllib.request.urlopen(u,timeout=25) as f:b=f.read();r.update(status=f.status,final_url=f.url)\\n (p/'eu2023_1803.html').write_bytes(b);r.update(path=str(p/'eu2023_1803.html'),sha256=hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest(),bytes=len(b))\\nexcept Exception as e:r.update(access_status='unavailable',error=str(e))\\n(p/'eu-access.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\\\\\\\\n');print(r)\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"{'id': 'eu2023_1803', 'url': 'https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32023R1803', 'retrieved_at': '2026-10-03T01:05:57.801400+00:00', 'status': 202, 'final_url': 'https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32023R1803', 'path': 'docs/design/research/p08-v1/eu2023_1803.html', 'sha256': 'e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855', 'bytes': 0}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_15\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"The applicable AASB 9 and AASB 7 texts are now retained. AASB 9 supplies the missing amortised-cost and effective-interest support. FASB returned 403, the Ministry of Finance route returned 502, and EUR-Lex returned no text; those routes provide no comparator authority. I’ll implement the supported Australian slice and record the comparison gaps explicitly.\\n\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\ns=Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.txt').read_text().splitlines()\\nfor a,b in [(420,431),(765,794),(2492,2518)]: print('\\\\\\\\n'.join(s[a:b]))\\ns=Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb7.txt').read_text().splitlines()\\nfor a,b in [(274,306),(493,521),(150,164)]:print('\\\\\\\\n'.join(s[a:b]))\\nPY\\nsed -n '306,323p' docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex\\nsed -n '348,360p' docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\ns=Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.txt').read_text().splitlines()\\nfor a,b in [(420,431),(765,794),(2492,2518)]: print('\\\\\\\\n'.join(s[a:b]))\\ns=Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb7.txt').read_text().splitlines()\\nfor a,b in [(274,306),(493,521),(150,164)]:print('\\\\\\\\n'.join(s[a:b]))\\nPY\\nsed -n '306,323p' docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex\\nsed -n '348,360p' docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"        accordingly, is within the scope of this Standard. Other contracts to which paragraph 2.4 applies are\\n        evaluated to determine whether they were entered into and continue to be held for the purpose of the receipt\\n        or delivery of the non-financial item in accordance with the entity’s expected purchase, sale or usage\\n        requirements and, accordingly, whether they are within the scope of this Standard.\\n2.7     A written option to buy or sell a non-financial item that can be settled net in cash or another financial\\n        instrument, or by exchanging financial instruments, in accordance with paragraph 2.6(a) or 2.6(d) is within\\n        the scope of this Standard. Such a contract cannot be entered into for the purpose of the receipt or delivery\\n        of the non-financial item in accordance with the entity’s expected purchase, sale or usage requirements.\\n\\n\\nChapter 3 Recognition and derecognition\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nAASB 9-compiled                                            15                                              STANDARD\\n                                  Authorised Version F2023C00399 registered 02/05/2023\\n\\n        Option to designate a financial asset at fair value through profit or loss\\n4.1.5   Despite paragraphs 4.1.1–4.1.4, an entity may, at initial recognition, irrevocably designate a financial\\n        asset as measured at fair value through profit or loss if doing so eliminates or significantly reduces a\\n        measurement or recognition inconsistency (sometimes referred to as an ‘accounting mismatch’) that\\n        would otherwise arise from measuring assets or liabilities or recognising the gains and losses on them\\n        on different bases (see paragraphs B4.1.29–B4.1.32).\\n\\n4.2 Classification of financial liabilities\\n4.2.1   An entity shall classify all financial liabilities as subsequently measured at amortised cost, except for:\\n        (a)       financial liabilities at fair value through profit or loss. Such liabilities, including derivatives\\n                  that are liabilities, shall be subsequently measured at fair value.\\n        (b)       financial liabilities that arise when a transfer of a financial asset does not qualify for\\n                  derecognition or when the continuing involvement approach applies. Paragraphs 3.2.15 and\\n                  3.2.17 apply to the measurement of such financial liabilities.\\n        (c)       financial guarantee contracts. After initial recognition, an issuer of such a contract shall\\n                  (unless paragraph 4.2.1(a) or (b) applies) subsequently measure it at the higher of:\\n                  (i)        the amount of the loss allowance determined in accordance with Section 5.5 and\\n                  (ii)       the amount initially recognised (see paragraph 5.1.1) less, when appropriate, the\\n                             cumulative amount of income recognised in accordance with the principles of\\n                             AASB 15.\\n        (d)       commitments to provide a loan at a below-market interest rate. An issuer of such a\\n                  commitment shall (unless paragraph 4.2.1(a) applies) subsequently measure it at the higher\\n                                 collateral held or other credit enhancements that are integral to the contractual\\n                                 terms. There is a presumption that the expected life of a financial instrument can\\n                                 be estimated reliably. However, in those rare cases when it is not possible to\\n                                 reliably estimate the expected life of a financial instrument, the entity shall use the\\n                                 remaining contractual term of the financial instrument.\\n\\ncredit-adjusted effective        The rate that exactly discounts the estimated future cash payments or receipts\\ninterest rate                    through the expected life of the financial asset to the amortised cost of a\\n                                 financial asset that is a purchased or originated credit-impaired financial\\n                                 asset. When calculating the credit-adjusted effective interest rate, an entity shall\\n                                 estimate the expected cash flows by considering all contractual terms of the\\n\\n\\n\\nAASB 9-compiled                                             44                                                APPENDIX A\\n                                   Authorised Version F2023C00399 registered 02/05/2023\\n\\n                               financial asset (for example, prepayment, extension, call and similar options) and\\n                               expected credit losses. The calculation includes all fees and points paid or\\n                               received between parties to the contract that are an integral part of the effective\\n                               interest rate (see paragraphs B5.4.1‒B5.4.3), transaction costs, and all other\\n                               premiums or discounts. There is a presumption that the cash flows and the\\n                               expected life of a group of similar financial instruments can be estimated reliably.\\n                               However, in those rare cases when it is not possible to reliably estimate the cash\\n                               flows or the remaining life of a financial instrument (or group of financial\\n                               instruments), the entity shall use the contractual cash flows over the full\\n         instruments into classes that are appropriate to the nature of the information disclosed and that take into\\n         account the characteristics of those financial instruments. An entity shall provide sufficient information to\\n         permit reconciliation to the line items presented in the statement of financial position.\\n\\n\\nSignificance of financial instruments for financial position and\\nperformance\\n7        An entity shall disclose information that enables users of its financial statements to evaluate the\\n         significance of financial instruments for its financial position and performance.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nAASB 7-compiled                                            7                                              STANDARD\\n                                  Authorised Version F2023C00392 registered 01/05/2023\\n\\n        Statement of financial position\\n        Categories of financial assets and financial liabilities\\n8       The carrying amounts of each of the following categories, as specified in AASB 9, shall be disclosed either\\n        in the statement of financial position or in the notes:\\n        (a)       financial assets measured at fair value through profit or loss, showing separately (i) those\\n                  designated as such upon initial recognition or subsequently in accordance with paragraph 6.7.1 of\\n                  AASB 9; (ii) those measured as such in accordance with the election in paragraph 3.3.5 of\\n                  AASB 9; (iii) those measured as such in accordance with the election in paragraph 33A of\\n                  AASB 132 and (iv) those mandatorily measured at fair value through profit or loss in accordance\\n                  with AASB 9.\\n        (b)–(d)   [deleted]\\n        (e)       financial liabilities at fair value through profit or loss, showing separately (i) those designated as\\n                  such upon initial recognition or subsequently in accordance with paragraph 6.7.1 of AASB 9 and\\n                  (ii) those that meet the definition of held for trading in AASB 9.\\n        (f)       financial assets measured at amortised cost.\\n        (g)       financial liabilities measured at amortised cost.\\n        (b)         the carrying amount of the loans payable in default at the end of the reporting period; and\\n        (c)         whether the default was remedied, or the terms of the loans payable were renegotiated, before the\\n                    financial statements were authorised for issue.\\n19      If, during the period, there were breaches of loan agreement terms other than those described in\\n        paragraph 18, an entity shall disclose the same information as required by paragraph 18 if those breaches\\n        permitted the lender to demand accelerated repayment (unless the breaches were remedied, or the terms of\\n        the loan were renegotiated, on or before the end of the reporting period).\\n\\n        Statement of comprehensive income\\n        Items of income, expense, gains or losses\\n20      An entity shall disclose the following items of income, expense, gains or losses either in the statement of\\n        comprehensive income or in the notes:\\n        (a)         net gains or net losses on:\\n                    (i)        financial assets or financial liabilities measured at fair value through profit or loss,\\n                               showing separately those on financial assets or financial liabilities designated as such\\n                               upon initial recognition or subsequently in accordance with paragraph 6.7.1 of\\n                               AASB 9, and those on financial assets or financial liabilities that are mandatorily\\n                               measured at fair value through profit or loss in accordance with AASB 9 (eg financial\\n                               liabilities that meet the definition of held for trading in AASB 9). For financial\\n                               liabilities designated as at fair value through profit or loss, an entity shall show\\n\\n\\n\\nAASB 7-compiled                                              11                                           STANDARD\\n                                    Authorised Version F2023C00392 registered 01/05/2023\\n\\n                              separately the amount of gain or loss recognised in other comprehensive income and\\n                              the amount recognised in profit or loss.\\n\\nAASB 7-compiled                                            4                                           CONTENTS\\n                                  Authorised Version F2023C00392 registered 01/05/2023\\n\\nComparison with IFRS 7\\nAASB 7 Financial Instruments: Disclosures as amended incorporates IFRS 7 Financial Instruments: Disclosures as\\nissued and amended by the International Accounting Standards Board (IASB). Australian-specific paragraphs (which\\nare not included in IFRS 7) are identified with the prefix “Aus”. Paragraphs that apply only to not-for-profit entities\\nbegin by identifying their limited applicability.\\n\\n\\nTier 1\\nFor-profit entities complying with AASB 7 also comply with IFRS 7.\\nNot-for-profit entities’ compliance with IFRS 7 will depend on whether any “Aus” paragraphs that specifically apply\\n\\n\\\\subsection{State Variables}\\\\label{sec:statevarsnotat}\\n\\nState Variables (states) describe the state of a contract at a certain point in time $t$ during its lifetime. Examples of such states are the (outstanding) Notional Principal, the applicable Nominal Interest Rate, or the current Contract Performance. The ACTUS dictionary (\\\\url{https://github.com/actusfrf/actus-dictionary/blob/master/actus-dictionary-states.json}) defines all states and provides further information on their data type, format, etc.\\n\\nIn general, states represent certain terms of a contract that change along the contract lifetime according to either scheduled events or unscheduled events. Therefore, states representing a contractual term carry the exact same names as their term-counterpart.\\n\\nStates are written in their short form representation with first letter capitalized, printed in bold, and indexed with time.\\n\\n\\\\begin{example}[State Variables]\\n$\\\\svar{Nt}{t}$ refers to the state \\\\textit{Notional Principal} observed at time $t$.\\n\\\\end{example}\\n\\n\\n\\\\subsection{Contract Events}\\\\label{sec:events}\\n\\nA Contract Event (event) $e_t^k$ refers to any contractually scheduled or unscheduled event at a certain time $t$ and of a certain type $k$. Contract events mark specific points in time during the lifetime of a contract at which a cash flow is being exchanged (see section \\\\ref{sec:pof}) or the states of the contract are being updated (see section \\\\ref{sec:stf}). The dictionary lists and describes all the event types $k$ defined by the ACTUS standards (\\\\url{https://github.com/actusfrf/actus-dictionary/blob/master/actus-dictionary-event-types.json}). Throughout this document event types $k$ are written in the short form as defined in the dictionary.\\n\\n\\\\end{example}\\n\\n\\n\\\\subsection{Payoff Functions}\\\\label{sec:pof}\\n\\nPayoff Functions (POF) define how the cash flow $c\\\\in\\\\Real$ for a certain event $e_t^k$ is being derived from current states and from the contract terms. If necessary, the resulting cash flow can be indexed with the event time $c_t$. These functions are specific to a certain event and contract. POFs are written according to the following pattern \\\\pof{[event type]}{[contract type]} where [event type] and [contract type] refer to the respective event and contract to which the STF belongs.\\n\\n\\\\begin{example}[Payoff Functions]\\nThe POF for an IP event $e_t^{IP}$ and PAM contract is written as \\\\pof{IP}{PAM} with $\\\\fev{e_t^{IP}}=\\\\pof{IP}{PAM}$.\\n\\\\end{example}\\n\\n\\n\\\\subsection{Date/Time}\\\\label{sec:time}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"cat > scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py <<'PY'\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Bounded, exact AASB issuer compound-bond lifecycle (P08).\\n\\nEligibility and fair value/yield inputs are explicit synthetic assumptions, not\\ninferred accounting opinions. Annual calendar periods only; no market model.\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom datetime import date\\nfrom fractions import Fraction\\nfrom hashlib import sha256\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport json\\nimport re\\n\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nREGISTER = 'docs/design/research/p08-v1/authority-register.json'\\nREQUIRED = ('recognition', 'classification', 'split', 'measurement', 'interest',\\n            'redemption', 'conversion', 'note_carrying', 'note_interest')\\nACCOUNTS = ('cash', 'liability', 'conversion_equity', 'share_equity',\\n            'opening_equity', 'interest_expense')\\n\\n\\nclass Unsupported(ValueError):\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"A fact, source, or event is outside the explicitly supported slice.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef rational(value):\\n    if isinstance(value, (bool, float)) or not isinstance(value, (str, int, Fraction)):\\n        raise Unsupported('amounts and rates require exact integer/rational inputs')\\n    try:\\n        return Fraction(value)\\n    except (ValueError, ZeroDivisionError) as exc:\\n        raise Unsupported('invalid rational') from exc\\n\\n\\ndef iso(value):\\n    try:\\n        result = date.fromisoformat(value)\\n        if result.isoformat() \\\"'!= value:\\n            raise ValueError('\\\"'noncanonical date')\\n        return result\\n    except (ValueError, TypeError) as exc:\\n        raise Unsupported('canonical ISO date required') from exc\\n\\n\\ndef wire(value):\\n    if isinstance(value, Fraction):\\n        return str(value)\\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\\n        return {key: wire(val) for key, val in value.items()}\\n    if isinstance(value, (list, tuple)):\\n        return [wire(val) for val in value]\\n    return value\\n\\n\\ndef normal(value):\\n    return re.sub(r'\\\\\\\\s+', ' ', value).strip()\\n\\n\\nclass AuthorityBook:\\n    def __init__(self, root=ROOT, records=None):\\n        self.root = Path(root)\\n        self.records = deepcopy(records) if records is not None else json.loads(\\n            (self.root / REGISTER).read_text())\\n        self.validate()\\n\\n    def validate(self):\\n        d = self.records\\n        if d.get('schema_version') \\\"'!= '\\\"'accdsl.p08.authority.v1':\\n            raise Unsupported('authority schema')\\n        self.sources = {r['id']: r for r in d['authorities']}\\n        self.claims = {r['id']: r for r in d['claims']}\\n        if len(self.sources) \\\"'!= len(d['\\\"'authorities']) or len(self.claims) \\\"'!= len(d['\\\"'claims']):\\n            raise Unsupported('duplicate authority or claim')\\n        for s in self.sources.values():\\n            if s['access_status'] \\\"'!= '\\\"'inspected_primary':\\n                continue\\n            if s.get('kind') \\\"'!= '\\\"'primary_standard' or not s.get('inspected_at'):\\n                raise Unsupported('uninspected or non-primary authority')\\n            for key in ('retained', 'text'):\\n                p = Path(s[key]['path'])\\n                if p.is_absolute() or '..' in p.parts or (self.root / p).is_symlink():\\n                    raise Unsupported('unsafe source path')\\n                try:\\n                    actual = sha256((self.root / p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\\n                except OSError as exc:\\n                    raise Unsupported('missing source') from exc\\n                if actual \\\"'!= s[key]['\\\"'sha256']:\\n                    raise Unsupported('source hash mismatch')\\n            iso(s['period_start_inclusive']); iso(s['period_start_exclusive'])\\n        for c in self.claims.values():\\n            s = self.sources.get(c['authority_id'])\\n            if not s or s['access_status'] \\\"'!= '\\\"'inspected_primary':\\n                raise Unsupported('claim lacks inspected primary source')\\n            pages = (self.root / s['text']['path']).read_text().split('\\\\\\\\f')\\n            for a in c['anchors']:\\n                if type(a['pdf_page']) is not int or not 1 <= a['pdf_page'] <= len(pages):\\n                    raise Unsupported('invalid anchor page')\\n                page = normal(pages[a['pdf_page'] - 1])\\n                if normal(a['quote']) not in page or a['paragraph'] not in s['inspected_paragraphs']:\\n                    raise Unsupported('unresolvable quote/paragraph')\\n        if any(c not in self.claims for c in REQUIRED):\\n            raise Unsupported('missing lifecycle authority')\\n        if set(d['note_links']) \\\"'!= {'\\\"'financing_carrying', 'financing_interest', 'financing_equity'}:\\n            raise Unsupported('note schema')\\n        for links in d['note_links'].values():\\n            if not links or any(link not in self.claims for link in links):\\n                raise Unsupported('unresolved note claim')\\n\\n    def admit(self, contract):\\n        # Revalidate so a caller cannot bypass source checks by mutating records.\\n        self.validate()\\n        for key in REQUIRED:\\n            s = self.sources[self.claims[key]['authority_id']]\\n            if (contract.jurisdiction \\\"'!= s['\\\"'jurisdiction'] or contract.basis \\\"'!= '\\\"'AASB'\\n                    or contract.tier \\\"'!= s['\\\"'tier'] or contract.entity_scope \\\"'!= s['\\\"'entity_scope']):\\n                raise Unsupported('authority jurisdiction/entity/tier mismatch')\\n            for year in range(iso(contract.issue_date).year,\\n                              iso(contract.issue_date).year + contract.years):\\n                start = date(year, 1, 1)\\n                if not iso(s['period_start_inclusive']) <= start < iso(s['period_start_exclusive']):\\n                    raise Unsupported('edition outside reporting-period start')\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass Contract:\\n    entity: str = 'SyntheticIssuer'\\n    book: str = 'statutory'\\n    currency: str = 'AUD'\\n    functional_currency: str = 'AUD'\\n    jurisdiction: str = 'AU'\\n    basis: str = 'AASB'\\n    tier: str = 'Tier 1'\\n    entity_scope: str = 'for-profit'\\n    issue_date: str = '2024-01-01'\\n    years: int = 2\\n    principal: str = '100'\\n    proceeds: str = '100'\\n    instrument_fair_value: str = '100'\\n    annual_coupon: str = '5'\\n    comparable_yield: str = '1/10'\\n    conversion_shares: int = 10\\n    conversion_right: str = 'maturity_only_fixed_for_fixed_nonputtable_ordinary'\\n    measurement: str = 'amortised_cost'\\n    unsupported_features: tuple = ()\\n\\n    def validate(self):\\n        if not self.entity or not self.book or not re.fullmatch('[A-Z]{3}', self.currency):\\n            raise Unsupported('entity/book/currency required')\\n        if self.currency \\\"'!= self.functional_currency:\\n            raise Unsupported('\\\"'FX unsupported')\\n        if (type(self.years) is not int or not 1 <= self.years <= 10\\n                or type(self.conversion_shares) is not int or self.conversion_shares <= 0):\\n            raise Unsupported('invalid term or shares')\\n        start = iso(self.issue_date)\\n        if (start.month, start.day) \\\"'!= (1, 1):\\n            raise Unsupported('\\\"'annual calendar periods only')\\n        if self.conversion_right \\\"'!= '\\\"'maturity_only_fixed_for_fixed_nonputtable_ordinary':\\n            raise Unsupported('unsupported conversion terms')\\n        if self.measurement \\\"'!= '\\\"'amortised_cost' or self.unsupported_features:\\n            raise Unsupported('fees/tax/options/modifications/default and other features excluded')\\n        p, proceeds, fair, coupon, rate = map(rational, (\\n            self.principal, self.proceeds, self.instrument_fair_value,\\n            self.annual_coupon, self.comparable_yield))\\n        if p <= 0 or proceeds <= 0 or coupon < 0 or rate < 0 or proceeds \\\"'!= fair:\\n            raise Unsupported('\\\"'positive principal/proceeds, fair-value proceeds and nonnegative coupon/yield required')\\n        liability = sum((coupon / (1 + rate) ** n for n in range(1, self.years + 1)), Fraction(0))\\n        liability += p / (1 + rate) ** self.years\\n        if liability > proceeds:\\n            raise Unsupported('negative residual equity: assumptions need reassessment')\\n        return liability\\n\\n    def coupon_dates(self):\\n        y = iso(self.issue_date).year\\n        return [date(y + i, 12, 31).isoformat() for i in range(self.years)]\\n\\n\\nclass BondBook:\\n    def __init__(self, contract, authority=None, opening_cash='20'):\\n        liability = contract.validate()\\n        self.authority = authority or AuthorityBook()\\n        self.authority.admit(contract)\\n        self.contract = contract\\n        self.initial_liability = liability\\n        opening = rational(opening_cash)\\n        if opening < 0:\\n            raise Unsupported('negative opening funding')\\n        self._ledger = {k: Fraction(0) for k in ACCOUNTS}\\n        self._ledger.update(cash=opening, opening_equity=-opening)\\n        self._journal = []\\n        self._used = set()\\n        self._position = 0\\n        self._shares = 0\\n        self._principal = Fraction(0)\\n        self._events = [('issue', contract.issue_date)]\\n        for day in contract.coupon_dates():\\n            self._events.extend([('accrue', day), ('coupon', day)])\\n        self._events.append(('settle', contract.coupon_dates()[-1]))\\n\\n    @property\\n    def state(self):\\n        return deepcopy({'ledger': self._ledger, 'position': self._position,\\n                         'shares': self._shares, 'principal_outstanding': self._principal,\\n                         'journal': self._journal, 'used_event_ids': sorted(self._used)})\\n\\n    def apply(self, event_id, kind, day):\\n        if not isinstance(event_id, str) or not event_id.strip() or event_id in self._used:\\n            raise Unsupported('missing/duplicate event identity')\\n        iso(day)\\n        if self._position >= len(self._events):\\n            raise Unsupported('already settled')\\n        expected, expected_day = self._events[self._position]\\n        if day \\\"'!= expected_day or (kind != expected and not (expected == '\\\"'settle' and kind in ('redeem', 'convert'))):\\n            raise Unsupported('out-of-order or conflicting event')\\n        c = self.contract\\n        ledger = deepcopy(self._ledger)\\n        shares, principal = self._shares, self._principal\\n        postings = {}\\n        claims = []\\n        if kind == 'issue':\\n            postings = {'cash': rational(c.proceeds), 'liability': -self.initial_liability,\\n                        'conversion_equity': -(rational(c.proceeds) - self.initial_liability)}\\n            principal = rational(c.principal)\\n            claims = ['recognition', 'classification', 'split']\\n        elif kind == 'accrue':\\n            interest = -ledger['liability'] * rational(c.comparable_yield)\\n            postings = {'interest_expense': interest, 'liability': -interest}\\n            claims = ['measurement', 'interest']\\n        elif kind == 'coupon':\\n            coupon = rational(c.annual_coupon)\\n            postings = {'liability': coupon, 'cash': -coupon}\\n            claims = ['measurement', 'redemption']\\n        elif kind in ('redeem', 'convert'):\\n            carrying = -ledger['liability']\\n            if carrying \\\"'!= rational(c.principal):\\n                raise Unsupported('\\\"'maturity liability does not equal principal')\\n            postings = {'liability': carrying, 'cash' if kind == 'redeem' else 'share_equity': -carrying}\\n            if kind == 'convert':\\n                shares += c.conversion_shares\\n            principal = Fraction(0)\\n            claims = ['redemption' if kind == 'redeem' else 'conversion']\\n        else:\\n            raise Unsupported('unsupported event')\\n        for account, amount in postings.items():\\n            ledger[account] += amount\\n        if sum(postings.values()) or sum(ledger.values()) or ledger['cash'] < 0 or ledger['liability'] > 0:\\n            raise Unsupported('journal/state/funding invariant')\\n        # Commit only after all validation, including funding and measurement.\\n        entry = {'id': event_id, 'kind': kind, 'date': day, 'entity': c.entity,\\n                 'book': c.book, 'currency': c.currency, 'postings_debit_positive': postings,\\n                 'claims': claims, 'state_after': deepcopy(ledger)}\\n        self._ledger, self._shares, self._principal = ledger, shares, principal\\n        self._journal.append(entry)\\n        self._used.add(event_id)\\n        self._position += 1\\n        return deepcopy(entry)\\n\\n    def notes(self):\\n        periods = []\\n        opening_carrying = Fraction(0)\\n        for year in range(iso(self.contract.issue_date).year,\\n                          iso(self.contract.issue_date).year + self.contract.years):\\n            rows = [x for x in self._journal if x['date'].startswith(str(year))]\\n            if not rows:\\n                continue\\n            def movement(kind, account):\\n                return sum((x['postings_debit_positive'].get(account, Fraction(0))\\n                            for x in rows if x['kind'] == kind), Fraction(0))\\n            issued = -movement('issue', 'liability')\\n            interest = movement('accrue', 'interest_expense')\\n            coupons = movement('coupon', 'liability')\\n            settled = movement('redeem', 'liability') + movement('convert', 'liability')\\n            closing = -rows[-1]['state_after']['liability']\\n            if opening_carrying + issued + interest - coupons - settled \\\"'!= closing:\\n                raise Unsupported('\\\"'note roll-forward mismatch')\\n            periods.append({'period_start': f'{year}-01-01', 'period_end': f'{year}-12-31',\\n                            'opening_liability': opening_carrying, 'issue_liability': issued,\\n                            'interest_expense': interest, 'coupons': coupons, 'settlement_liability': settled,\\n                            'closing_liability': closing, 'event_ids': [x['id'] for x in rows]})\\n            opening_carrying = closing\\n        return {'periods': periods, 'links': deepcopy(self.authority.records['note_links']),\\n                'mandatory_disclosure_scope': 'selected carrying amount and interest only; not a complete AASB 7 note',\\n                'conversion_equity': -self._ledger['conversion_equity'],\\n                'issued_share_equity': -self._ledger['share_equity'], 'issued_shares': self._shares}\\n\\n\\ndef run_case(contract=None, settlement='redeem', opening_cash='20', authority=None):\\n    c = contract or Contract()\\n    book = BondBook(c, authority, opening_cash)\\n    book.apply('issue', 'issue', c.issue_date)\\n    for i, day in enumerate(c.coupon_dates(), 1):\\n        book.apply(f'accrue-{i}', 'accrue', day)\\n        book.apply(f'coupon-{i}', 'coupon', day)\\n    book.apply('settlement', settlement, c.coupon_dates()[-1])\\n    return wire({'contract': vars(c), 'settlement': settlement, 'opening_cash': rational(opening_cash),\\n                 'initial_liability': book.initial_liability, 'state': book.state, 'notes': book.notes()})\\n\\n\\ndef compare_same_facts(contract=None, authority=None):\\n    c = contract or Contract()\\n    facts = wire(vars(c))\\n    # Hash common economics without changing terms for an unavailable rule set.\\n    economic = {k: v for k, v in facts.items() if k not in ('basis', 'jurisdiction', 'tier', 'entity_scope', 'book')}\\n    digest = sha256(json.dumps(economic, sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()\\n    case = run_case(c, authority=authority)\\n    rows = [{'standard': 'AASB', 'jurisdiction': 'AU', 'facts_sha256': digest,\\n             'status': 'supported_bounded', 'initial_liability': case['initial_liability'],\\n             'initial_equity': str(rational(c.proceeds) - rational(case['initial_liability'])),\\n             'total_interest': case['state']['ledger']['interest_expense'],\\n             'claims': list(REQUIRED)}]\\n    for standard, jurisdiction, missing in [\\n        ('US GAAP', 'US', 'Applicable ASC 470/815 and ASU 2020-06 text, adoption and exceptions uninspected; official PDF 403.'),\\n        ('ASBE', 'CN', 'Official CAS 22/37 text, applicable edition and entity transition uninspected; MoF route 502.'),\\n        ('EU-endorsed IFRS', 'EU', 'Applicable endorsed IAS 32/IFRS 9 text and amendments uninspected; EUR-Lex returned empty 202.')]:\\n        rows.append({'standard': standard, 'jurisdiction': jurisdiction, 'facts_sha256': digest,\\n                     'status': 'unresolved', 'initial_liability': None, 'initial_equity': None,\\n                     'total_interest': None, 'claims': [], 'missing': missing})\\n    return {'economic_facts': economic, 'rows': rows, 'supported_difference': None,\\n            'criterion_status': 'incomplete: no second inspected applicable standard',\\n            'interpretation': 'No numerical difference or equivalence is established; Australian adoption is not universal IFRS authority.'}\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"cat > scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py <<'PY'\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Bounded, exact AASB issuer compound-bond lifecycle (P08).\\n\\nEligibility and fair value/yield inputs are explicit synthetic assumptions, not\\ninferred accounting opinions. Annual calendar periods only; no market model.\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom datetime import date\\nfrom fractions import Fraction\\nfrom hashlib import sha256\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport json\\nimport re\\n\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nREGISTER = 'docs/design/research/p08-v1/authority-register.json'\\nREQUIRED = ('recognition', 'classification', 'split', 'measurement', 'interest',\\n            'redemption', 'conversion', 'note_carrying', 'note_interest')\\nACCOUNTS = ('cash', 'liability', 'conversion_equity', 'share_equity',\\n            'opening_equity', 'interest_expense')\\n\\n\\nclass Unsupported(ValueError):\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"A fact, source, or event is outside the explicitly supported slice.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef rational(value):\\n    if isinstance(value, (bool, float)) or not isinstance(value, (str, int, Fraction)):\\n        raise Unsupported('amounts and rates require exact integer/rational inputs')\\n    try:\\n        return Fraction(value)\\n    except (ValueError, ZeroDivisionError) as exc:\\n        raise Unsupported('invalid rational') from exc\\n\\n\\ndef iso(value):\\n    try:\\n        result = date.fromisoformat(value)\\n        if result.isoformat() \\\"'!= value:\\n            raise ValueError('\\\"'noncanonical date')\\n        return result\\n    except (ValueError, TypeError) as exc:\\n        raise Unsupported('canonical ISO date required') from exc\\n\\n\\ndef wire(value):\\n    if isinstance(value, Fraction):\\n        return str(value)\\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\\n        return {key: wire(val) for key, val in value.items()}\\n    if isinstance(value, (list, tuple)):\\n        return [wire(val) for val in value]\\n    return value\\n\\n\\ndef normal(value):\\n    return re.sub(r'\\\\\\\\s+', ' ', value).strip()\\n\\n\\nclass AuthorityBook:\\n    def __init__(self, root=ROOT, records=None):\\n        self.root = Path(root)\\n        self.records = deepcopy(records) if records is not None else json.loads(\\n            (self.root / REGISTER).read_text())\\n        self.validate()\\n\\n    def validate(self):\\n        d = self.records\\n        if d.get('schema_version') \\\"'!= '\\\"'accdsl.p08.authority.v1':\\n            raise Unsupported('authority schema')\\n        self.sources = {r['id']: r for r in d['authorities']}\\n        self.claims = {r['id']: r for r in d['claims']}\\n        if len(self.sources) \\\"'!= len(d['\\\"'authorities']) or len(self.claims) \\\"'!= len(d['\\\"'claims']):\\n            raise Unsupported('duplicate authority or claim')\\n        for s in self.sources.values():\\n            if s['access_status'] \\\"'!= '\\\"'inspected_primary':\\n                continue\\n            if s.get('kind') \\\"'!= '\\\"'primary_standard' or not s.get('inspected_at'):\\n                raise Unsupported('uninspected or non-primary authority')\\n            for key in ('retained', 'text'):\\n                p = Path(s[key]['path'])\\n                if p.is_absolute() or '..' in p.parts or (self.root / p).is_symlink():\\n                    raise Unsupported('unsafe source path')\\n                try:\\n                    actual = sha256((self.root / p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\\n                except OSError as exc:\\n                    raise Unsupported('missing source') from exc\\n                if actual \\\"'!= s[key]['\\\"'sha256']:\\n                    raise Unsupported('source hash mismatch')\\n            iso(s['period_start_inclusive']); iso(s['period_start_exclusive'])\\n        for c in self.claims.values():\\n            s = self.sources.get(c['authority_id'])\\n            if not s or s['access_status'] \\\"'!= '\\\"'inspected_primary':\\n                raise Unsupported('claim lacks inspected primary source')\\n            pages = (self.root / s['text']['path']).read_text().split('\\\\\\\\f')\\n            for a in c['anchors']:\\n                if type(a['pdf_page']) is not int or not 1 <= a['pdf_page'] <= len(pages):\\n                    raise Unsupported('invalid anchor page')\\n                page = normal(pages[a['pdf_page'] - 1])\\n                if normal(a['quote']) not in page or a['paragraph'] not in s['inspected_paragraphs']:\\n                    raise Unsupported('unresolvable quote/paragraph')\\n        if any(c not in self.claims for c in REQUIRED):\\n            raise Unsupported('missing lifecycle authority')\\n        if set(d['note_links']) \\\"'!= {'\\\"'financing_carrying', 'financing_interest', 'financing_equity'}:\\n            raise Unsupported('note schema')\\n        for links in d['note_links'].values():\\n            if not links or any(link not in self.claims for link in links):\\n                raise Unsupported('unresolved note claim')\\n\\n    def admit(self, contract):\\n        # Revalidate so a caller cannot bypass source checks by mutating records.\\n        self.validate()\\n        for key in REQUIRED:\\n            s = self.sources[self.claims[key]['authority_id']]\\n            if (contract.jurisdiction \\\"'!= s['\\\"'jurisdiction'] or contract.basis \\\"'!= '\\\"'AASB'\\n                    or contract.tier \\\"'!= s['\\\"'tier'] or contract.entity_scope \\\"'!= s['\\\"'entity_scope']):\\n                raise Unsupported('authority jurisdiction/entity/tier mismatch')\\n            for year in range(iso(contract.issue_date).year,\\n                              iso(contract.issue_date).year + contract.years):\\n                start = date(year, 1, 1)\\n                if not iso(s['period_start_inclusive']) <= start < iso(s['period_start_exclusive']):\\n                    raise Unsupported('edition outside reporting-period start')\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass Contract:\\n    entity: str = 'SyntheticIssuer'\\n    book: str = 'statutory'\\n    currency: str = 'AUD'\\n    functional_currency: str = 'AUD'\\n    jurisdiction: str = 'AU'\\n    basis: str = 'AASB'\\n    tier: str = 'Tier 1'\\n    entity_scope: str = 'for-profit'\\n    issue_date: str = '2024-01-01'\\n    years: int = 2\\n    principal: str = '100'\\n    proceeds: str = '100'\\n    instrument_fair_value: str = '100'\\n    annual_coupon: str = '5'\\n    comparable_yield: str = '1/10'\\n    conversion_shares: int = 10\\n    conversion_right: str = 'maturity_only_fixed_for_fixed_nonputtable_ordinary'\\n    measurement: str = 'amortised_cost'\\n    unsupported_features: tuple = ()\\n\\n    def validate(self):\\n        if not self.entity or not self.book or not re.fullmatch('[A-Z]{3}', self.currency):\\n            raise Unsupported('entity/book/currency required')\\n        if self.currency \\\"'!= self.functional_currency:\\n            raise Unsupported('\\\"'FX unsupported')\\n        if (type(self.years) is not int or not 1 <= self.years <= 10\\n                or type(self.conversion_shares) is not int or self.conversion_shares <= 0):\\n            raise Unsupported('invalid term or shares')\\n        start = iso(self.issue_date)\\n        if (start.month, start.day) \\\"'!= (1, 1):\\n            raise Unsupported('\\\"'annual calendar periods only')\\n        if self.conversion_right \\\"'!= '\\\"'maturity_only_fixed_for_fixed_nonputtable_ordinary':\\n            raise Unsupported('unsupported conversion terms')\\n        if self.measurement \\\"'!= '\\\"'amortised_cost' or self.unsupported_features:\\n            raise Unsupported('fees/tax/options/modifications/default and other features excluded')\\n        p, proceeds, fair, coupon, rate = map(rational, (\\n            self.principal, self.proceeds, self.instrument_fair_value,\\n            self.annual_coupon, self.comparable_yield))\\n        if p <= 0 or proceeds <= 0 or coupon < 0 or rate < 0 or proceeds \\\"'!= fair:\\n            raise Unsupported('\\\"'positive principal/proceeds, fair-value proceeds and nonnegative coupon/yield required')\\n        liability = sum((coupon / (1 + rate) ** n for n in range(1, self.years + 1)), Fraction(0))\\n        liability += p / (1 + rate) ** self.years\\n        if liability > proceeds:\\n            raise Unsupported('negative residual equity: assumptions need reassessment')\\n        return liability\\n\\n    def coupon_dates(self):\\n        y = iso(self.issue_date).year\\n        return [date(y + i, 12, 31).isoformat() for i in range(self.years)]\\n\\n\\nclass BondBook:\\n    def __init__(self, contract, authority=None, opening_cash='20'):\\n        liability = contract.validate()\\n        self.authority = authority or AuthorityBook()\\n        self.authority.admit(contract)\\n        self.contract = contract\\n        self.initial_liability = liability\\n        opening = rational(opening_cash)\\n        if opening < 0:\\n            raise Unsupported('negative opening funding')\\n        self._ledger = {k: Fraction(0) for k in ACCOUNTS}\\n        self._ledger.update(cash=opening, opening_equity=-opening)\\n        self._journal = []\\n        self._used = set()\\n        self._position = 0\\n        self._shares = 0\\n        self._principal = Fraction(0)\\n        self._events = [('issue', contract.issue_date)]\\n        for day in contract.coupon_dates():\\n            self._events.extend([('accrue', day), ('coupon', day)])\\n        self._events.append(('settle', contract.coupon_dates()[-1]))\\n\\n    @property\\n    def state(self):\\n        return deepcopy({'ledger': self._ledger, 'position': self._position,\\n                         'shares': self._shares, 'principal_outstanding': self._principal,\\n                         'journal': self._journal, 'used_event_ids': sorted(self._used)})\\n\\n    def apply(self, event_id, kind, day):\\n        if not isinstance(event_id, str) or not event_id.strip() or event_id in self._used:\\n            raise Unsupported('missing/duplicate event identity')\\n        iso(day)\\n        if self._position >= len(self._events):\\n            raise Unsupported('already settled')\\n        expected, expected_day = self._events[self._position]\\n        if day \\\"'!= expected_day or (kind != expected and not (expected == '\\\"'settle' and kind in ('redeem', 'convert'))):\\n            raise Unsupported('out-of-order or conflicting event')\\n        c = self.contract\\n        ledger = deepcopy(self._ledger)\\n        shares, principal = self._shares, self._principal\\n        postings = {}\\n        claims = []\\n        if kind == 'issue':\\n            postings = {'cash': rational(c.proceeds), 'liability': -self.initial_liability,\\n                        'conversion_equity': -(rational(c.proceeds) - self.initial_liability)}\\n            principal = rational(c.principal)\\n            claims = ['recognition', 'classification', 'split']\\n        elif kind == 'accrue':\\n            interest = -ledger['liability'] * rational(c.comparable_yield)\\n            postings = {'interest_expense': interest, 'liability': -interest}\\n            claims = ['measurement', 'interest']\\n        elif kind == 'coupon':\\n            coupon = rational(c.annual_coupon)\\n            postings = {'liability': coupon, 'cash': -coupon}\\n            claims = ['measurement', 'redemption']\\n        elif kind in ('redeem', 'convert'):\\n            carrying = -ledger['liability']\\n            if carrying \\\"'!= rational(c.principal):\\n                raise Unsupported('\\\"'maturity liability does not equal principal')\\n            postings = {'liability': carrying, 'cash' if kind == 'redeem' else 'share_equity': -carrying}\\n            if kind == 'convert':\\n                shares += c.conversion_shares\\n            principal = Fraction(0)\\n            claims = ['redemption' if kind == 'redeem' else 'conversion']\\n        else:\\n            raise Unsupported('unsupported event')\\n        for account, amount in postings.items():\\n            ledger[account] += amount\\n        if sum(postings.values()) or sum(ledger.values()) or ledger['cash'] < 0 or ledger['liability'] > 0:\\n            raise Unsupported('journal/state/funding invariant')\\n        # Commit only after all validation, including funding and measurement.\\n        entry = {'id': event_id, 'kind': kind, 'date': day, 'entity': c.entity,\\n                 'book': c.book, 'currency': c.currency, 'postings_debit_positive': postings,\\n                 'claims': claims, 'state_after': deepcopy(ledger)}\\n        self._ledger, self._shares, self._principal = ledger, shares, principal\\n        self._journal.append(entry)\\n        self._used.add(event_id)\\n        self._position += 1\\n        return deepcopy(entry)\\n\\n    def notes(self):\\n        periods = []\\n        opening_carrying = Fraction(0)\\n        for year in range(iso(self.contract.issue_date).year,\\n                          iso(self.contract.issue_date).year + self.contract.years):\\n            rows = [x for x in self._journal if x['date'].startswith(str(year))]\\n            if not rows:\\n                continue\\n            def movement(kind, account):\\n                return sum((x['postings_debit_positive'].get(account, Fraction(0))\\n                            for x in rows if x['kind'] == kind), Fraction(0))\\n            issued = -movement('issue', 'liability')\\n            interest = movement('accrue', 'interest_expense')\\n            coupons = movement('coupon', 'liability')\\n            settled = movement('redeem', 'liability') + movement('convert', 'liability')\\n            closing = -rows[-1]['state_after']['liability']\\n            if opening_carrying + issued + interest - coupons - settled \\\"'!= closing:\\n                raise Unsupported('\\\"'note roll-forward mismatch')\\n            periods.append({'period_start': f'{year}-01-01', 'period_end': f'{year}-12-31',\\n                            'opening_liability': opening_carrying, 'issue_liability': issued,\\n                            'interest_expense': interest, 'coupons': coupons, 'settlement_liability': settled,\\n                            'closing_liability': closing, 'event_ids': [x['id'] for x in rows]})\\n            opening_carrying = closing\\n        return {'periods': periods, 'links': deepcopy(self.authority.records['note_links']),\\n                'mandatory_disclosure_scope': 'selected carrying amount and interest only; not a complete AASB 7 note',\\n                'conversion_equity': -self._ledger['conversion_equity'],\\n                'issued_share_equity': -self._ledger['share_equity'], 'issued_shares': self._shares}\\n\\n\\ndef run_case(contract=None, settlement='redeem', opening_cash='20', authority=None):\\n    c = contract or Contract()\\n    book = BondBook(c, authority, opening_cash)\\n    book.apply('issue', 'issue', c.issue_date)\\n    for i, day in enumerate(c.coupon_dates(), 1):\\n        book.apply(f'accrue-{i}', 'accrue', day)\\n        book.apply(f'coupon-{i}', 'coupon', day)\\n    book.apply('settlement', settlement, c.coupon_dates()[-1])\\n    return wire({'contract': vars(c), 'settlement': settlement, 'opening_cash': rational(opening_cash),\\n                 'initial_liability': book.initial_liability, 'state': book.state, 'notes': book.notes()})\\n\\n\\ndef compare_same_facts(contract=None, authority=None):\\n    c = contract or Contract()\\n    facts = wire(vars(c))\\n    # Hash common economics without changing terms for an unavailable rule set.\\n    economic = {k: v for k, v in facts.items() if k not in ('basis', 'jurisdiction', 'tier', 'entity_scope', 'book')}\\n    digest = sha256(json.dumps(economic, sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()\\n    case = run_case(c, authority=authority)\\n    rows = [{'standard': 'AASB', 'jurisdiction': 'AU', 'facts_sha256': digest,\\n             'status': 'supported_bounded', 'initial_liability': case['initial_liability'],\\n             'initial_equity': str(rational(c.proceeds) - rational(case['initial_liability'])),\\n             'total_interest': case['state']['ledger']['interest_expense'],\\n             'claims': list(REQUIRED)}]\\n    for standard, jurisdiction, missing in [\\n        ('US GAAP', 'US', 'Applicable ASC 470/815 and ASU 2020-06 text, adoption and exceptions uninspected; official PDF 403.'),\\n        ('ASBE', 'CN', 'Official CAS 22/37 text, applicable edition and entity transition uninspected; MoF route 502.'),\\n        ('EU-endorsed IFRS', 'EU', 'Applicable endorsed IAS 32/IFRS 9 text and amendments uninspected; EUR-Lex returned empty 202.')]:\\n        rows.append({'standard': standard, 'jurisdiction': jurisdiction, 'facts_sha256': digest,\\n                     'status': 'unresolved', 'initial_liability': None, 'initial_equity': None,\\n                     'total_interest': None, 'claims': [], 'missing': missing})\\n    return {'economic_facts': economic, 'rows': rows, 'supported_difference': None,\\n            'criterion_status': 'incomplete: no second inspected applicable standard',\\n            'interpretation': 'No numerical difference or equivalence is established; Australian adoption is not universal IFRS authority.'}\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_18\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfor name, needles in [('aasb9',['3.1.1   An entity','4.2.1   An entity','effective interest method      The method']),('aasb7',['8       The carrying','total interest expense'])]:\\n s=Path(f'docs/design/research/p08-v1/{name}.txt').read_text()\\n for needle in needles:\\n  i=s.find(needle); print(name,'page',s[:i].count('\\\\\\\\f')+1,repr(s[i:i+1250]))\\ns=Path('docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt').read_text()\\nfor needle in ['28      The issuer','35      Interest','AG32      On conversion']:\\n i=s.find(needle);print('132 page',s[:i].count('\\\\\\\\f')+1,repr(s[i:i+750]))\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_18\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfor name, needles in [('aasb9',['3.1.1   An entity','4.2.1   An entity','effective interest method      The method']),('aasb7',['8       The carrying','total interest expense'])]:\\n s=Path(f'docs/design/research/p08-v1/{name}.txt').read_text()\\n for needle in needles:\\n  i=s.find(needle); print(name,'page',s[:i].count('\\\\\\\\f')+1,repr(s[i:i+1250]))\\ns=Path('docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt').read_text()\\nfor needle in ['28      The issuer','35      Interest','AG32      On conversion']:\\n i=s.find(needle);print('132 page',s[:i].count('\\\\\\\\f')+1,repr(s[i:i+750]))\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"aasb9 page 10 '3.1.1   An entity shall recognise a financial asset or a financial liability in its statement of financial position\\\\n        when, and only when, the entity becomes party to the contractual provisions of the instrument (see\\\\n        paragraphs B3.1.1 and B3.1.2). When an entity first recognises a financial asset, it shall classify it in\\\\n        accordance with paragraphs 4.1.1–4.1.5 and measure it in accordance with paragraphs 5.1.1–5.1.3.\\\\n        When an entity first recognises a financial liability, it shall classify it in accordance with\\\\n        paragraphs 4.2.1 and 4.2.2 and measure it in accordance with paragraph 5.1.1.\\\\n\\\\n        Regular way purchase or sale of financial assets\\\\n3.1.2   A regular way purchase or sale of financial assets shall be recognised and derecognised, as applicable,\\\\n        using trade date accounting or settlement date accounting (see paragraphs B3.1.3–B3.1.6).\\\\n\\\\n3.2 Derecognition of financial assets\\\\n3.2.1   In consolidated financial statements, paragraphs 3.2.2–3.2.9, B3.1.1, B3.1.2 and B3.2.1–B3.2.17 are applied\\\\n        at a consolidated level. Hence, an entity first consolidates all subsidiaries in accordance with AASB 10 and\\\\n        then applies those paragraphs to the resulting group.\\\\n3.2.2   Before ev'\\naasb9 page 16 '4.2.1   An entity shall classify all financial liabilities as subsequently measured at amortised cost, except for:\\\\n        (a)       financial liabilities at fair value through profit or loss. Such liabilities, including derivatives\\\\n                  that are liabilities, shall be subsequently measured at fair value.\\\\n        (b)       financial liabilities that arise when a transfer of a financial asset does not qualify for\\\\n                  derecognition or when the continuing involvement approach applies. Paragraphs 3.2.15 and\\\\n                  3.2.17 apply to the measurement of such financial liabilities.\\\\n        (c)       financial guarantee contracts. After initial recognition, an issuer of such a contract shall\\\\n                  (unless paragraph 4.2.1(a) or (b) applies) subsequently measure it at the higher of:\\\\n                  (i)        the amount of the loss allowance determined in accordance with Section 5.5 and\\\\n                  (ii)       the amount initially recognised (see paragraph 5.1.1) less, when appropriate, the\\\\n                             cumulative amount of income recognised in accordance with the principles of\\\\n                             AASB 15.\\\\n        (d)       commitments to provide a loan at a below'\\naasb9 page 45 'effective interest method      The method that is used in the calculation of the amortised cost of a financial\\\\n                               asset or a financial liability and in the allocation and recognition of the interest\\\\n                               revenue or interest expense in profit or loss over the relevant period.\\\\n\\\\neffective interest rate        The rate that exactly discounts estimated future cash payments or receipts through\\\\n                               the expected life of the financial asset or financial liability to the gross carrying\\\\n                               amount of a financial asset or to the amortised cost of a financial liability.\\\\n                               When calculating the effective interest rate, an entity shall estimate the expected\\\\n                               cash flows by considering all the contractual terms of the financial instrument (for\\\\n                               example, prepayment, extension, call and similar options) but shall not consider\\\\n                               the expected credit losses. The calculation includes all fees and points paid or\\\\n                               received between parties to the contract that are an integral part of the effective\\\\n        '\\naasb7 page 8 '8       The carrying amounts of each of the following categories, as specified in AASB 9, shall be disclosed either\\\\n        in the statement of financial position or in the notes:\\\\n        (a)       financial assets measured at fair value through profit or loss, showing separately (i) those\\\\n                  designated as such upon initial recognition or subsequently in accordance with paragraph 6.7.1 of\\\\n                  AASB 9; (ii) those measured as such in accordance with the election in paragraph 3.3.5 of\\\\n                  AASB 9; (iii) those measured as such in accordance with the election in paragraph 33A of\\\\n                  AASB 132 and (iv) those mandatorily measured at fair value through profit or loss in accordance\\\\n                  with AASB 9.\\\\n        (b)–(d)   [deleted]\\\\n        (e)       financial liabilities at fair value through profit or loss, showing separately (i) those designated as\\\\n                  such upon initial recognition or subsequently in accordance with paragraph 6.7.1 of AASB 9 and\\\\n                  (ii) those that meet the definition of held for trading in AASB 9.\\\\n        (f)       financial assets measured at amortised cost.\\\\n        (g)       financial liabilities measured at amortised cost.\\\\n     '\\naasb7 page 12 'total interest expense (calculated using the effective interest method) for\\\\n                  financial assets that are measured at amortised cost or that are measured at fair value through\\\\n                  other comprehensive income in accordance with paragraph 4.1.2A of AASB 9 (showing these\\\\n                  amounts separately); or financial liabilities that are not measured at fair value through profit or\\\\n                  loss.\\\\n        (c)       fee income and expense (other than amounts included in determining the effective interest rate)\\\\n                  arising from:\\\\n                  (i)         financial assets and financial liabilities that are not at fair value through profit or loss;\\\\n                              and\\\\n                  (ii)        trust and other fiduciary activities that result in the holding or investing of assets on\\\\n                              behalf of individuals, trusts, retirement benefit plans, and other institutions.\\\\n        (d)       [deleted]\\\\n        (e)       [deleted]\\\\n20A     An entity shall disclose an analysis of the gain or loss recognised in the statement of comprehensive income\\\\n        arising from the derecognition of financial assets measured at amortised cost, showing separatel'\\n132 page 13 '28      The issuer of a non-derivative financial instrument shall evaluate the terms of the financial\\\\n        instrument to determine whether it contains both a liability and an equity component. Such\\\\n        components shall be classified separately as financial liabilities, financial assets or equity instruments\\\\n        in accordance with paragraph 15.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nAASB 132-compiled                                          13                                                STANDARD\\\\n                                  Authorised Version F2023C00406 registered 04/05/2023\\\\n\\\\x0c29      An entity recognises separately the components of a financial instrument that (a) creates a financial liability\\\\n        of the entity and (b) grants an option to the holder of t'\\n132 page 15 '35      Interest, dividends, losses and gains relating to a financial instrument or a component that is a\\\\n        financial liability shall be recognised as income or expense in profit or loss. Distributions to holders of\\\\n        an equity instrument shall be recognised by the entity directly in equity. Transaction costs of an\\\\n        equity transaction shall be accounted for as a deduction from equity.\\\\n35A     Income tax relating to distributions to holders of an equity instrument and to transaction costs of an equity\\\\n        transaction shall be accounted for in accordance with AASB 112 Income Taxes.\\\\n36      The classification of a financial instrument as a financial liability or an equity instrument determines\\\\n        whether interest, d'\\n132 page 25 'AG32      On conversion of a convertible instrument at maturity, the entity derecognises the liability component and\\\\n          recognises it as equity. The original equity component remains as equity (although it may be transferred\\\\n          from one line item within equity to another). There is no gain or loss on conversion at maturity.\\\\nAG33      When an entity extinguishes a convertible instrument before maturity through an early redemption or\\\\n          repurchase in which the original conversion privileges are unchanged, the entity allocates the consideration\\\\n          paid and any transaction costs for the repurchase or redemption to the liability and equity components of the\\\\n          instrument at the date of the transaction. The meth'\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_19\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"cat > /tmp/p08_register.py <<'PY'\\nimport json,hashlib,datetime,pathlib,re\\nroot=pathlib.Path('.');base=root/'docs/design/research/p08-v1'\\ndef asset(p):return {'path':p,'sha256':hashlib.sha256((root/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()}\\ndef norm(s):return re.sub(r'\\\\\\\\s+',' ',s).strip()\\nnow=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()\\nrecords=json.loads((base/'access-records.json').read_text())+[json.loads((base/'eu-access.json').read_text())]\\nauthorities=[]\\nfor id,stem,title,pars in [\\n ('aasb132','docs/design/research/standards/aasb132','AASB 132 Financial Instruments: Presentation',['22','22A','25–27','28–32','35','AG30–AG35']),\\n ('aasb9','docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9','AASB 9 Financial Instruments',['3.1.1','3.3.1–3.3.3','4.2.1','5.1.1','Appendix A: amortised cost','Appendix A: effective interest']),\\n ('aasb7','docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb7','AASB 7 Financial Instruments: Disclosures',['7','8(g)','20(b)'])]:\\n access=next((a for a in records if a['id']==id),None)\\n authorities.append({'id':id,'title':title,'issuer':'Australian Accounting Standards Board','kind':'primary_standard','access_status':'inspected_primary',\\n 'official_url':access['url'] if access else 'https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB132_08-15_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf',\\n 'retrieved_at':access['retrieved_at'] if access else '2026-10-02 (prior archive; time not recorded)',\\n 'inspected_at':now,'retained':asset(stem+'.pdf'),'text':asset(stem+'.txt'),\\n 'edition':'31 December 2022 compilation; amendments through 15 December 2022',\\n 'jurisdiction':'AU','entity_scope':'for-profit','tier':'Tier 1',\\n 'period_start_inclusive':'2023-01-01','period_start_exclusive':'2026-07-01',\\n 'transition_conditions':'Use this compilation only for annual periods with start in the stated interval; no optional early adoption of subsequent amendments. Synthetic cases use calendar 2024 and 2025.',\\n 'applicability_anchor':'Cover and compilation preamble; Comparison with IAS/IFRS, Tier 1.',\\n 'inspected_paragraphs':pars,'limits':'Only listed paragraphs inspected. Official Australian adoption; no universal IFRS jurisdiction conclusion.'})\\nclaims=[]\\ndef claim(id,source,para,quote,meaning):\\n s=next(x for x in authorities if x['id']==source)\\n pages=(root/s['text']['path']).read_text().split('\\\\\\\\f')\\n found=[i+1 for i,p in enumerate(pages) if norm(quote) in norm(p)]\\n if len(found)\\\"'!=1:raise ValueError((id,found))\\n claims.append({'\\\"'id':id,'authority_id':source,'anchors':[{'paragraph':para,'pdf_page':found[0],'quote':quote}],\\n                'supported_statement':meaning,'status':'inspected_primary_conditional'})\\nclaim('recognition','aasb9','3.1.1','when, and only when, the entity becomes party to the contractual provisions of the instrument','Recognise the contractual financial liability when the issuer becomes party; proceeds are assumed equal to instrument fair value.')\\nclaim('fair_value','aasb9','5.1.1','measure a financial asset or financial liability at its fair value plus or minus','Initial measurement uses fair value; this slice assumes proceeds equal fair value and no transaction costs.')\\nclaim('classification','aasb132','22','fixed number of its own equity instruments in exchange for a fixed amount of cash or another financial asset is an equity instrument.','Fixed-for-fixed equity classification, conditional on ordinary non-puttable shares, functional currency and exclusion of settlement alternatives/contingencies.')\\nclaim('split','aasb132','AG30–AG35','On initial recognition, the fair value of the liability component is the present value of the contractually determined stream of future cash flows','AG31(a): discount liability cash flows at comparable non-convertible market yield; paragraphs 28–32 allocate residual proceeds to equity.')\\nclaim('residual_equity','aasb132','28–32','the equity component is assigned the residual amount after deducting from the fair value of the instrument as a whole','Paragraph 31 supplies residual allocation. Equity is not remeasured; retained on expiry is a local deduction from paragraph 22 and liability-only extinguishment, not a separate quoted redemption rule.')\\nclaim('measurement','aasb9','4.2.1','An entity shall classify all financial liabilities as subsequently measured at amortised cost, except for:','Ordinary liability uses amortised cost. Exclude fair-value designation/trading, derivatives, guarantees, transfer liabilities, below-market commitments and business-combination contingent consideration.')\\nclaim('interest','aasb9','Appendix A: effective interest','the allocation and recognition of the interest revenue or interest expense in profit or loss over the relevant period.','Effective-interest method allocates interest expense; use opening liability times the assumed exact annual effective yield.')\\nclaim('amortised_cost','aasb9','Appendix A: amortised cost','minus the principal repayments, plus or minus the cumulative amortisation using the effective interest method','Amortised cost roll-forward follows contractual payments and cumulative effective-interest amortisation.')\\nclaim('redemption','aasb9','3.3.1–3.3.3','when, and only when, it is extinguished – ie when the obligation specified in the contract is discharged or cancelled or expires.','Remove the discharged liability; paragraph 3.3.3 difference is profit/loss. At this exact maturity, consideration equals carrying amount, so zero settlement gain/loss.')\\nclaim('conversion','aasb132','AG30–AG35','On conversion of a convertible instrument at maturity, the entity derecognises the liability component and recognises it as equity.','AG32: maturity conversion reclassifies liability to equity, leaves original equity within equity and produces no gain/loss.')\\nclaim('note_carrying','aasb7','8(g)','financial liabilities measured at amortised cost.','8(g), read with paragraph 8 lead-in: disclose carrying amounts of financial liabilities at amortised cost on the face or in notes.')\\nclaim('note_interest','aasb7','20(b)','total interest revenue and total interest expense (calculated using the effective interest method)','20(b): disclose effective-interest totals for liabilities not measured at fair value through profit/loss. This is selected note content only.')\\nresearch={'source':'docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex','sha256':hashlib.sha256((root/'docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex').read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\\n 'inspected_sections':['State Variables (sec:statevarsnotat)','Contract Events (sec:events)','Payoff Functions (sec:pof)'],\\n 'decision':'defer integration; no ACTUS algorithm, schedule, code or forecast mechanism adopted',\\n 'support':'Retained technical specification distinguishes dated events, state changes and cash-flow functions.',\\n 'transfer_limit':'Implementation uses an explicit user-specified annual schedule and local accounting transitions. No ACTUS compatibility, official-code equivalence, empirical evaluation or company-simulation validity claim. Broader method/theory/evaluation and code audit required before future adoption.'}\\nqueue=[]\\nfor method,boundary,missing,interpretation,case,req,gap in [\\n ('revenue','single contract, performance obligation, delivery/collection','Applicable AASB 15/ASC 606/ASBE 14 primary paragraphs','Distinct promises, variable-consideration constraint and timing','Two obligations, advance cash, partial delivery and refund','MC15/MC19','G4/G7'),\\n ('tax','current tax and one temporary difference','Applicable AASB 112/ASC 740/ASBE 18 and tax law','Tax base, enacted rates and deferred-tax recoverability','Two-year depreciation difference and loss carryforward','MC15/MC19','G4/G7'),\\n ('leases','lessee recognition through one remeasurement','Applicable AASB 16/ASC 842/ASBE 21','Renewal certainty, lease term and discount-rate reset','Lease commencement, coupon, changed option and termination','MC15/MC19','G4/G7'),\\n ('FX','foreign-currency payable then settlement; translation separate','Applicable AASB 121/ASC 830/ASBE 19','Functional currency, monetary classification and translation reserves','Year-end payable remeasurement and next-year cash settlement','MC06/MC15/MC19','G4/G7'),\\n ('complex_groups','acquisition, NCI, eliminations and disposal','Applicable AASB 3/10/128, ASC 805/810 and ASBE 20/33','Control, substantive rights, common control and NCI measurement','Mid-year acquisition, intercompany sale, partial disposal','MC06/MC15/MC19','G4/G7'),\\n ('bonds','extend issuer lifecycle beyond fixed maturity conversion','Applicable ASC 470/815, ASU 2020-06 and ASBE 22/37; further AASB provisions','Early repurchase, inducement, modification, embedded terms, default and disclosure completeness','Early cash repurchase with separated consideration and reconciled equity','MC17/MC19/MC29/MC30','G4/G7/G8')]:\\n queue.append(dict(method=method,operation_boundary=boundary,missing_authority=missing,unresolved_interpretation=interpretation,next_exact_case=case,requirements=req.split('/'),gaps=gap.split('/'),status='internal_follow_up'))\\nd={'schema_version':'accdsl.p08.authority.v1','created_at':now,'authorities':authorities,'claims':claims,'access_attempts':records,\\n 'note_links':{'financing_carrying':['note_carrying','measurement'],'financing_interest':['note_interest','interest'],'financing_equity':['split','residual_equity','conversion']},\\n 'research':[research],'method_queue':queue,'prior_blocks':'The historical FASB ASU 2015-11 and MoF index blocks remain preserved in standards-support.json. New attempts above are distinct document routes; no challenge bypass or unchanged retry.',\\n 'uninspected_standards':['ASC 470/815 and ASU 2020-06','ASBE 22/37','EU-endorsed IAS 32/IFRS 9'],\\n 'inspection_limit':'Quotes and page resolution establish retained support, not exh